  "about": "Interpreted from the satellite view (metre grid), the street frames and the Commons photographs: a salmon-terracotta stucco church on a long north-east axis. Big terracotta ribbed dome over the crossing at the south-west end; at the north-east end a front of four stepped concentric arches (lighter at each edge) with the saint in a niche, a stained-glass arch, a flat porch on columns and a cross, flanked by two drum towers with blue-grey domes; a pale beige roof deck with two strips of solar panels; a two-storey terracotta block along the south-east side; an ivy wall along the street with a hedge at its foot; paving in rings in front.",
